WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.110
Field devices form the connection between digital control and the physical process.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:12.672
Sensors measure conditions such as temperature, pressure, flow, level, speed, vibration, or position.

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:20.139
Instrumentation may condition, convert, or transmit those measurements so a controller can use them reliably.

00:00:20.139 --> 00:00:24.891
Actuators perform physical work in response to control signals.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:35.074
A valve actuator changes flow, a motor drives machinery, a variable-frequency drive adjusts speed, and a relay changes an electrical circuit.

00:00:35.074 --> 00:00:41.184
Some devices combine measurement, local logic, diagnostics, and actuation in one package.

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:50.462
Field signals may be discrete, indicating states such as open or closed, or analog, representing a range of values.

00:00:50.462 --> 00:00:58.834
They can travel through direct input and output wiring, serial links, fieldbus networks, industrial Ethernet, or gateways.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:07.659
The architecture must account for both networked devices and equipment that never appears as a conventional IP endpoint.

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:18.295
Field-device integrity is essential because bad data can lead to a bad control decision, while an incorrect output can affect equipment immediately.

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:26.215
A failed sensor, wiring problem, calibration error, configuration mistake, or cyber event may produce similar symptoms.

00:01:26.215 --> 00:01:31.872
Diagnosis requires process history, device health, controller evidence, and physical inspection.

00:01:31.872 --> 00:01:43.865
Security measures include accurate inventory, controlled physical access, protected cabinets and wiring, documented calibration, approved configuration tools, and monitoring of unexpected device or communication changes.

00:01:43.865 --> 00:01:52.238
Safety protections and fail-safe behavior should be engineered independently rather than assumed to come from cybersecurity controls.

00:01:52.238 --> 00:01:56.990
Field devices remind us why ICS security is operational.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:04.457
A digital message can open a valve, start a motor, or change an electrical state.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:12.830
Defenders must understand the device function, expected operating range, failure mode, and safe response before recommending actions.
